    "abstract": "QLoRA backpropagates through a frozen 4-bit quantized pretrained language model into Low-Rank Adapters, reducing memory enough to finetune a 65B model on a single 48GB GPU while preserving 16-bit finetuning performance. It introduces 4-bit NormalFloat (NF4), Double Quantization, and Paged Optimizers. The resulting Guanaco models reach 99.3% of ChatGPT's performance on the Vicuna benchmark after 24 hours of finetuning on one GPU.",
    "domain": "NLP",
    "key_claims": [
      "NF4 is an information-theoretically optimal 4-bit data type for normally distributed weights and outperforms FP4 and Int4.",
      "Double Quantization reduces quantization-constant overhead from 0.5 to about 0.127 bits per parameter.",
      "QLoRA with NF4 matches 16-bit full finetuning and 16-bit LoRA on academic benchmarks.",
      "LoRA must be applied to all linear layers to match full finetuning.",
      "Guanaco 65B reaches 99.3% of ChatGPT on the Vicuna benchmark, trained in 24 hours on a single 48GB GPU."
    ],
